wayland: make simulateUserActivity() restart the idle timeouts, so the system sleeps again after a wakeup.

PowerDevil suspends after the profile's idle time, through a KIdleTime timeout. When the system
wakes up by itself and nobody touches it, it should sleep again after that time: PowerDevil calls
KIdleTime::simulateUserActivity() on resume for that (and when inhibitions change), but on Wayland
it did nothing. Each timeout's idle notification fires once, and only input re-arms it, so the
system stayed awake until someone came back (2.5 hours on the lock screen, on 2026-11-09).

Neither idle protocol can reset the idle time, so recreate the notifications: the compositor counts
each new one from its creation, as simulated activity does on X11. The dim and screen-off actions
firing again are harmless (both check whether they already did). The old notifications are deleted
after the event loop's current turn, since this can run from one of their own signals.

To turn it off, set RestartIdleTimers=false in the [Power] group of ~/.config/danylo-tweaksrc
(System Settings > Danylo's Linux Tweaks > Power & Battery), read each time.

Applied by scripts/patches/patch-library, see scripts/configure_hardware.

diff --git a/src/plugins/wayland/poller.cpp b/src/plugins/wayland/poller.cpp
index 86294fc..eafb724 100644
--- a/src/plugins/wayland/poller.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/wayland/poller.cpp
@@ -8,9 +8,14 @@
 #include <QDebug>
 #include <QGuiApplication>
 #include <QLoggingCategory>
+#include <QSettings>
+#include <QStandardPaths>
+#include <QTimer>
 #include <QWaylandClientExtensionTemplate>
 #include <QtWaylandClientVersion>
 
+#include <utility>
+
 #include "qwayland-ext-idle-notify-v1.h"
 #include "qwayland-idle.h"
 
@@ -190,6 +195,26 @@ int Poller::forcePollRequest()
 
 void Poller::simulateUserActivity()
 {
+    // ext-idle-notify has no request to reset the idle time. Recreate the timeouts instead: the
+    // compositor counts each new one from now. Otherwise a timeout that already fired (say, the one
+    // that suspends the system) stays fired until the next input, so after a wakeup nobody touches,
+    // the system never sleeps again. Unless turned off in System Settings > Danylo's Linux Tweaks.
+    const QSettings tweaks(QStandardPaths::writableLocation(QStandardPaths::GenericConfigLocation)
+                               + QStringLiteral("/danylo-tweaksrc"),
+                           QSettings::IniFormat);
+    if (!tweaks.value(QStringLiteral("Power/RestartIdleTimers"), true).toBool()) {
+        return;
+    }
+    const auto old = std::exchange(m_timeouts, {});
+    for (const auto &timeout : old) {
+        timeout->disconnect(this);
+    }
+    // This can run from one of their signals (resumed, through KIdleTime::resumingFromIdle), so
+    // delete them after it.
+    QTimer::singleShot(0, this, [old] {});
+    for (auto it = old.keyBegin(); it != old.keyEnd(); ++it) {
+        addTimeout(*it);
+    }
 }
 
 IdleTimeout* Poller::createTimeout(int timeout)
